  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASEAN EU-German Climate Action Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The &#xbf;ASEAN EU-German Climate Action Programme&#xbf; is jointly co-financed by the European Union and the Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development and implemented by GIZ as part of the BMZ project &#xbf;Climate Action Program&#xbf;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action is part of and contributes to the EU-ASEAN Green Initiative. The action aims to contribute to components 1 &#xbf;Horizontal Climate Change Component&#xbf; and 5 &#xbf;Clean, Affordable, Reliable, Sustainable and Modern Energy&#xbf;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Overall Objective of the Action is to improve ASEAN&#xbf;s capacity to promote regional cooperation for implementing ambitious climate policies and for accelerating the sustainable energy transition towards clean energy and greater energy efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Specific Objectives (outcomes) of the Action are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ASEAN&#xbf;s capacities to promote regional cooperation for implementing ambitious climate policies are enhanced.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ASEAN Member States (AMS) accelerate the transition towards renewable energy and greater energy efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
